SageMaker Domain details page. Each tab has a different purpose:

| Tab                       | What it means             | Simple explanation                                                                             |
| ------------------------- | ------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| ⚙️ **Domain settings**    | Main domain configuration | General settings and configuration for the entire SageMaker Domain                             |
| 👤 **User profiles**      | SageMaker users           | Create and manage users who can access SageMaker Studio and resources                          |
| 📦 **Space management**   | Workspaces                | Manage **Spaces**, which are shared or private environments for running SageMaker applications |
| 📱 **App Configurations** | Application setup         | Configure applications and tools that users can launch inside SageMaker                        |
| 🌐 **Environment**        | Network & infrastructure  | Configure the environment, such as networking, security, and other infrastructure settings     |
| 🧩 **Resources**          | Connected resources       | View and manage resources associated with the SageMaker Domain                                 |


===

Easy hierarchy
AWS Account
    ↓
SageMaker AI
    ↓
Domain 🏢
    ├── Domain settings ⚙️
    ├── User profiles 👤
    ├── Spaces 📦
    ├── App configurations 📱
    ├── Environment 🌐
    └── Resources 🧩

Most important for beginners: Start with User profiles. You create a user profile, then that user can access the SageMaker workspace and applications.

